#
# ── Findings (vs the screenshot-derived #41 option-C ranking) ───────────────
# 1. collect_residuals is the #1 symbol on EVERY content class (12-23%) —
#    the universal target. Ranking upgrade: collect first or jointly with
#    gather (they share the per-pixel WP + residual+tokenize shape).
# 2. gather_samples: 15-19% on screens/docs, only ~7.5-7.9% on photos
#    (photos use 50% sampling stride; screens/docs gather more relative
#    work). Confirms the SIMD chunk pays most on screenshots/documents.
# 3. WP predict_and_property 6-15% everywhere — third member of the same
#    per-pixel loop family; batching candidate per option-C item 3.
# 4. NEW: large-photo regime has a DIFFERENT #1 — dedup packed-key-sort
#    memcmp at 16.9% + Vec::from_iter 11.2% on the 12MP photo (~28%
#    combined). This is the predicted O(n log n) crossover from the
#    W44-137 triage of #41 Phase 1: inline hash-dedup, which lost at
#    1024^2, should be re-evaluated specifically at >=8MP photo sizes.
#    At 1MP photo memcmp is already 10.8%.
# 5. find_best_split residual: 15.1% on clic097 / 9.8% on city12mp even
#    post-hist-sub+rider (photos remain partially split-bound); screens/
#    docs 1.4-5.0% as established.
# 6. estimate_cost (select_best_rct trials) is a steady 4.5-9.0%
#    everywhere — previously untracked; worth a look after the top items
#    (it re-tokenizes the image per RCT candidate).
#
# Raw data: /tmp/gprof/{clic097,city12mp,noaa,mobile,terminal,imac_dark}
# .data (regenerate with the commands above; not committed).
#
# ── ADDENDUM: intra-function split (perf annotate + addr2line) ──────────────
# collect_residuals (terminal cell): 8.68% of CPU at the inlined
#   traverse_with_props (tree_learn.rs:7939) — per-pixel MA-tree walk
#   (property-compare branches); ~7.8% in copy_from_slice /
#   copy_nonoverlapping at :7849 + :7806 — per-pixel property-array
#   copies into the collection buffers.
# gather_samples (noaa cell): 22.2% of the function on ONE insn —
#   movdqu 0x3c0(%rsp) reload (stack scratch -> SoA push copies of
#   local_tokens/local_ebits/props), +14.6% on two loop-counter incs
#   (per-predictor / per-prop push loops).
# DESIGN CONSEQUENCE for the SIMD chunk: the wall is per-pixel DATA
# MOVEMENT (scratch->SoA copies, tree-walk branches) at least as much as
# predictor math. Row-buffered bulk extends (amortize the SoA pushes)
# and a vectorized/branchless traverse_with_props matter alongside the
# lane-per-predictor residual+tokenize from the #41 brief.
#
